Ghost Gate -- Tari Ootle 0.49.2 wallet minimum-value-promise patch

Stock walletd can read a stealth output's minimum value promise, but its transfer-statement RPC
cannot request a non-zero promise: the wallet SDK hard-codes every generated output witness to
zero. Ghost Gate needs the wallet to prove a gate-specific public floor while retaining custody of
the output keys. This narrow patch carries the caller's requested floor through the existing
wallet-owned statement path and rejects an impossible floor before locking inputs.

Apply from a clean Tari Ootle 0.49.2 source tree:

    git apply --recount -p1 C:/path/to/ghost-gate-public/docs/wallet-mvp-0492.patch

